chx:Research a res:ResearchProject ; rdfs:label "Digital signatures: SIGHASH, schnorr and ECDSA, recomputed against the standards and Bitcoin Core 31.1"@en ;
    sen0414:methodology "Primary source first: the chapter's named concepts from the book's own source at tag third_edition_print1. Then the official documentation for the current release and the PEPs the chapter's topics touch. Every source opened and read on 2026-10-15T02:32:21Z; every claim taken from text actually read; every behaviour executed under Python 3.14.4." ;
    res:hasResearchScope chx:Scope ; rdfs:member chx:P01, chx:P02, chx:P03, chx:P04, chx:P05, chx:P06, chx:P07, chx:P08, chx:P09, chx:P10, chx:P11, chx:P12, chx:P13, chx:P14, chx:P15, chx:P16, chx:P17, chx:P18, chx:P19, chx:P20, chx:P21, chx:P22, chx:P23, chx:P24, chx:P25, chx:P26, chx:P27, chx:P28, chx:P29, chx:P30, chx:P31, chx:P32, chx:P33, chx:P34, chx:P35, chx:P36, chx:P37, chx:P38, chx:P39, chx:P40, chx:P41, chx:P42, chx:P43, chx:P44, chx:P45, chx:P46, chx:P47, chx:P48, chx:P49, chx:P50, chx:P51, chx:P52, chx:P53, chx:P54, chx:P55, chx:P56, chx:P57, chx:P58, chx:P59, chx:P60, chx:P61, chx:P62, chx:P63, chx:P64, chx:P65, chx:P66 .
chx:Scope a res:ResearchScope ; res:hasResearchQuestion "How do the signatures of chapter 8 of Mastering Bitcoin's 3rd edition work (what a signature commits to through the SIGHASH flags, how schnorr and ECDSA signatures are made, serialized and protected by their nonces, and what segwit changed), which of its examples, figures and statements can be reproduced from the standards and by Bitcoin Core 31.1, and where has the software or the state of the proposals moved since the book went to print?" ; res:hasTimeWindow "Current as of 2026-10-15." .
